@startuml failover
title US-07: Failover - Leader crash, clean shutdown (compare-before-DEL), and follower takeover

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Evaluator\nInstance A\n(leader)" as A
participant "Evaluator\nInstance B\n(follower)" as B
database "Redis\nalert-evaluator:leader" as Redis
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Normal operation - compare-and-renew ==

A -> Kafka : emitting alerts normally
A -> Redis : SET alert-evaluator:leader $instance_a XX PX $TTL_MS\n(compare-and-renew: SET only if key exists AND value unchanged)
Redis --> A : OK (lease renewed)

note over A
  Compare-and-renew prevents a lagging slow instance
  from extending a lease it no longer owns.
  SET XX fails if the key has been acquired by a new leader.
end note

== Scenario 1: Leader crash (ungraceful) ==

A ->x A : crash — lease renewal stops — TTL counts down

loop follower polling
  B -> Redis : GET alert-evaluator:leader
  Redis --> B : $instance_a (lease still held)
end

note over Redis
  TTL expires.
  Key is automatically deleted by Redis.
end note

Redis -> Redis : key expired and deleted

B -> Redis : SET alert-evaluator:leader $instance_b NX PX $TTL_MS
Redis --> B : OK (lease acquired — Instance B is now leader)

note over B
  Failover complete within one TTL window.
  No manual intervention required.
  No duplicate alerts: B was not evaluating while A held the lease.
  Deterministic alert_id + ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING handles
  the case where A published to Kafka before crashing
  but did not commit the Kafka offset — B re-processes safely.
end note

B -> Kafka : emit alerts (new leader)

== Scenario 2: Clean shutdown (compare-before-DEL) ==

note over A
  Instance A is shutting down gracefully.
  Must NOT delete the lease if a new leader
  has already acquired it (race window).
end note

A -> Redis : Lua: if GET('alert-evaluator:leader') == $instance_a\nthen DEL('alert-evaluator:leader') end
Redis --> A : 1 (deleted own lease) or 0 (new leader holds it — skip DEL)

note over A
  Atomic compare-before-DEL via Lua script.
  If B already acquired the lease, DEL is skipped.
  B continues uninterrupted.
end note

@enduml
